// Fixture for a C variadic with a mixed fixed prefix
// (tests/build_hosted_helper.cmake, PHASE 7f.10).
//
// `mixed_var_sum(int, double, int, ...)` puts a floating value at argument
// position one and a floating tail at position three. On Win64 that is xmm1
// and xmm3 (plus the integer duplicate in rdx and r9); a class counter that
// starts at xmm0 would hand the callee the wrong registers. System V keeps
// separate class counters, so the same declaration must return the same sum
// there. The helper asserts the sum, so a wrong register is a wrong number.
extern "C" {
  fn mixed_var_sum(a: int, b: double, c: int, ...): double;
}

assertEq(mixed_var_sum(1, 2.5, 3, 4.5, 5), 16.0);

print("ffi variadic mixed ok");
